e for nurse practitioners</source><year>2006</year><month>1</month><volume>14</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16425517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-mjm12_1p31"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fix</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sexton</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Langenberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The association of nocturnal asthma with asthma severity</article-title><source>J Asthma</source><year>1997</year><volume>34</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9250257</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-mjm12_1p31"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colice</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Burgt</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Song</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Categorizing asthma severity</article-title><source>American journal of respiratory and critical care medicine</source><year>1999</year><month>12</month><volume>160</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1962</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10588614</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-mjm12_1p31"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Contopoulos-Ioannidis</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Manoli</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>Ioannidis</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Meta-analysis of the association of beta2-adrenergic receptor polymorphisms with asthma phenotypes</article-title><source>The Journal of allergy and clinical immunology</source><year>2005</year><day>May